# Nissth line-ending policy — Phase 11 (Fresh-Clone Hardening).
#
# Why this file exists: without it, a clone on a host with core.autocrlf=true
# materializes every text file with CRLF. The Expo test fixtures are parsed by
# LF-anchored regexes, so the Expo suite failed on a fresh clone while passing
# in the development directory. See
# AgentReports/Reports/2026-08-21_fresh-clone-build-failures.md (defect #2).
#
# Safe to apply: the index was measured uniformly LF (0 CRLF files outside
# Axiom/) before this file was added, so the baseline line normalizes nothing —
# it only pins the working-tree side.

* text=auto eol=lf

# Batch files are the one class that must keep CRLF. A .cmd with LF-only
# endings can misparse labels and goto on Windows. Applies to the two tracked
# Maven wrappers: Bindings/SpringBoot/mvnw.cmd and
# Bindings/SpringBoot/tests/fixture/mvnw.cmd.
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.bat text eol=crlf

# Deliberately NOT overridden: *.ps1 (PowerShell reads LF correctly) and the
# extensionless POSIX launchers (nissth-bridge, mvnw), which need the LF
# baseline to stay executable on macOS and Linux.

# Never run text filters over binaries.
*.pdf binary
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.jar binary
